# gnu-netcat disappeared from the ALARM repos; openbsd-netcat is the
# maintained replacement and provides the same `nc`.
openbsd-netcat

# ===
# GPU  -- Mali G610 driven by the panthor kernel driver
# ===
# panthor (kernel, in linux-fydetab) + panfrost gallium (mesa) + panvk (vulkan-panfrost).
# NOT used: the Rockchip vendor mali_kbase blob driver, libmali, or mesa-panfork-git
# -- panfork was the pre-panthor stopgap and is obsolete here.
#
# The CSF firmware comes from linux-firmware-other (pulled in by linux-firmware),
# which since 2026 ships arm/mali/arch10.8/mali_csffw.bin (a symlink to
# ../arch10.10/, one blob for arch 10.8/10.10/10.12) -- verified: CSF magic OK,
# header 0.3, version_hash 0x01050000, newer than the rkr4 blob. Our
# mali-G610-firmware-rkr4 package installs the SAME path and pacstrap fails on
# the file conflict, so it stays in the repo as a fallback but out of the image.
mesa
vulkan-panfrost

